---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
    title="Committee Code of Conduct"
    description="Code of Conduct for Committee Members"
>
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-black to-gray-900 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Committee Code of Conduct</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300">
        Code of Conduct for Committee Members
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="pt-16 pb-0 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <!-- Introduction -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">This Code of Conduct outlines the standards expected of all committee members to ensure the effective,
            professional, and harmonious management of Omagh Harriers A.C.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">1. General Principles</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Act in the best interests of Omagh Harriers A.C. and its members at all times.</li>
            <li>Foster an environment of respect, inclusion, and professionalism.</li>
            <li>Promote the values of fairness, integrity, and transparency within the club.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">2. Confidentiality</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Keep all discussions, documents, and sensitive information from committee meetings strictly confidential
              unless explicitly authorized for disclosure.
            </li>
            <li>Respect and protect the privacy of members, ensuring compliance with data protection laws.</li>
            <li>Do not use confidential information for personal gain or to undermine the club or its members.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">3. Expected Behaviours</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Attend and actively contribute to committee meetings and club events.</li>
            <li>Value and respect diverse opinions, even when they differ from your own.</li>
            <li>Avoid and disclose conflicts of interest that may compromise decision-making.</li>
            <li>Uphold the reputation of Omagh Harriers A.C. through positive and constructive representation.</li>
            <li>Refrain from any form of discriminatory, harassing, or offensive behaviour.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">4. Internal Digital Communication Media</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Use club-approved platforms (e.g., email, WhatsApp, Teams) for all committee communications to ensure
              consistency and accountability.
            </li>
            <li>Maintain professionalism in tone and language when communicating via digital channels.</li>
            <li>Ensure digital communications remain respectful, inclusive, and free from offensive or inappropriate
              content.
            </li>
            <li>Do not share confidential discussions, documents, or member information on digital platforms outside the
              committee without explicit authorization.
            </li>
            <li>Avoid engaging in public disputes or criticism of the club, its members, or its policies on social media or
              other digital forums.
            </li>
            <li>Report any misuse of digital communication channels to the Chairperson or relevant committee member.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">5. Handling Breaches of the Code</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Breaches will be addressed swiftly and fairly by the committee.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Complaints will be investigated impartially, ensuring all parties are treated with respect.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Sanctions for breaches may include:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-6">
            <li>Verbal or written warnings.</li>
            <li>Temporary suspension from the committee.</li>
            <li>Permanent removal from the committee, based on the severity of the breach.</li>
            <li>Serious or unlawful breaches may be escalated to external authorities, as necessary.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">6. Acknowledgement</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">By serving on the committee, you agree to adhere to this Code of Conduct, contributing to the club&rsquo;s trust,
            respect, and accountability.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3"><em>I hereby agree to abide by the terms and conditions outlined in the above Code of Conduct and commit to
            upholding the values and standards of Omagh Harriers A.C.</em></p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Reviewed and agreed by all members of the 2025 Committee.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6"><strong>Date Approved:</strong>&nbsp;3 December 2024<br/><strong>Approved By:</strong>&nbsp;N. Heaney
            (Chairperson)</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Logo -->
        <div class="mt-12 text-center">
          <img src="/omagh-harriers_black.png" alt="Omagh Harriers AC Logo" width="408" height="160" class="mx-auto" />
        </div>
        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <a
            href="/policies"
            class="inline-flex items-center text-black hover:text-amber transition-colors font-semibold"
          >
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"/>
            </svg>
            Back to Policies
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
